    'cookies.title' => 'Pit o Cuixa Cookie Policy',
    'cookies.desc' => 'This platform uses both first-party and third-party cookies, during the browsing session and on a permanent basis, to function properly, obtain traffic information, and remember users’ actions and preferences for future visits.',

    // ── Section 0 ────────
    'cookies.intro.title' => 'What Are Cookies?',
    'cookies.intro.paragraph1' => 'A cookie is a file that is downloaded to your computer or device when you access our platform. Cookies allow us to store and retrieve information about a user’s browsing habits or their device. Depending on the information they contain and how the device is used, cookies may be used to recognise the user.',
    'cookies.intro.paragraph2' => 'The cookies used by Last, or by a third party acting on its behalf, are associated only with an anonymous user and their computer. We do not store sensitive personally identifiable information in the cookies we use.',

    // ── Section 1 ────────
    'cookies.purpose.title' => 'Purpose',
    'cookies.purpose.paragraph1' => 'Thanks to cookies, it is possible for the Last server, or a third party acting on its behalf, to recognise the browser used by the user’s computer in order to facilitate browsing. They are also used to measure audience size, analyse traffic data, monitor progress and track the number of visits.',
    'cookies.purpose.paragraph2' => 'Likewise, the Last web servers and application can automatically detect the user’s IP address and domain name. All this information is recorded in a server activity log that enables data processing for statistical analysis. This includes the number of page impressions and visits to the web services and the application, among other things. In any case, this log is anonymised to prevent user identification.',

    // ── Section 2 ────────
    'cookies.types.title' => 'Types of Cookies',
    'cookies.types.paragraph1' => 'Our platform uses both first-party and third-party cookies for different purposes, including:',
    'cookies.types.item1' => 'First-party cookies: These are sent to your computer or device from our platform.',
    'cookies.types.item2' => 'Third-party cookies: These are sent to your computer or device from a domain or website that is not managed by us, but by another entity that processes the data obtained through the cookies.',
    'cookies.types.item3' => 'Session cookies: These cookies are designed to collect and store data while you access our platform.',
    'cookies.types.item4' => 'Persistent cookies: These cookies store data on the device and can be accessed and processed for a defined period of time, ranging from a few minutes to several years.',
    'cookies.types.item5' => 'Analytical cookies: These, whether managed by us or by third parties, allow us to quantify the number of users and perform statistical analysis of how users use our platform. We analyse browsing activity on our application in order to improve the services we offer.',
    'cookies.types.google_analytics' => 'We use Google Analytics to collect information anonymously and generate reports on website and application trends without identifying individual users. This allows our application to remember information that changes the appearance or behaviour of the site. The provider of this cookie is Google.',
    'cookies.types.google_ads' => 'We use Google AdWords to collect information anonymously and generate reports on visits generated through Google AdWords advertising without identifying individual users. In this way, our application sends information to Google to generate reports on the marketing campaigns launched. The provider of this cookie is Google.',
    'cookies.types.google' => 'We use Google to collect information anonymously and generate reports on visits generated through advertisements managed by Google without identifying individual users. Our platform sends information to Google to generate reports on the marketing campaigns launched. The provider of this cookie is Google.',
    'cookies.types.facebook' => 'We use Facebook to collect information anonymously and generate reports on visits generated through Facebook advertising without identifying individual users. Our application sends information to Facebook to generate reports on the marketing campaigns launched. The provider of this cookie is Facebook.',

    // ── Section 3 ────────
    'cookies.consent.title' => 'Consent',
    'cookies.consent.paragraph1' => 'We inform you that we may use cookies on your device provided that you have given your prior consent, except where cookies are necessary for browsing the application.',
    'cookies.consent.paragraph2' => 'The use of different cookies by our platform allows us to distinguish you from other users, provide you with a better experience and identify issues in order to improve our platform. If you give your consent, we will use cookies that allow us to learn more about your preferences.',
    'cookies.consent.paragraph3' => 'You can block or disable cookies that are not necessary for the use of our platform through your browser settings. If you block or disable them, you will still be able to use our platform, but some services may be limited and your experience may be less satisfactory.',
